{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6655710",
      "title": "Creating a New Component",
      "lectureOrder": 337,
      "videoOrder": 315,
      "sourceHash": "a5c292c36ea729665dae396e0be63666e27736e47dddd639b333dce63fbcdc7b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.46,
          "end": 4.14,
          "en": "-: Components are important, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.14,
          "end": 5.55,
          "en": "That is why we start with one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.55,
          "end": 7.2,
          "en": "with the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.2,
          "end": 9.93,
          "en": "It on one hand is a normal Angular component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.93,
          "end": 11.91,
          "en": "but on the other end it's also kind of special",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.91,
          "end": 14.67,
          "en": "because it serves us as our root component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.67,
          "end": 16.8,
          "en": "It's in the end listed here in the app module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 16.8,
          "end": 18.18,
          "en": "in this bootstrap array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 18.18,
          "end": 20.97,
          "en": "which tells Angular, \"Hey, this is a special component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 20.97,
          "end": 23.82,
          "en": "You should bootstrap the whole application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 23.82,
          "end": 26.43,
          "en": "with that component, being the root component.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 26.43,
          "end": 29.97,
          "en": "So all other components we create will not be added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.97,
          "end": 31.92,
          "en": "to the index html file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 31.92,
          "end": 34.71,
          "en": "Their selectors will not be added here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 34.71,
          "end": 38.79,
          "en": "Their selectors will be added to the app component HTML file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 38.79,
          "end": 41.91,
          "en": "because this is now the, well root component of our app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 41.91,
          "end": 44.01,
          "en": "where we add the other parts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 44.01,
          "end": 46.14,
          "en": "Enough talking about adding components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 46.14,
          "end": 48,
          "en": "Let's add one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 48,
          "end": 53,
          "en": "Let's say we want to output some information about a server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 53.58,
          "end": 54.9,
          "en": "We're building a backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 54.9,
          "end": 57.63,
          "en": "for our server management application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 57.63,
          "end": 60.69,
          "en": "and we want to output some server information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 60.69,
          "end": 62.94,
          "en": "So I will store this in a new folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 62.94,
          "end": 65.43,
          "en": "which is a SAP folder of the app folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 65.43,
          "end": 68.46000000000001,
          "en": "because generally in a Angular CLI project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 68.46000000000001,
          "end": 73.41,
          "en": "all your app related content will go into this app folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 73.41,
          "end": 74.88,
          "en": "I will name it \"server\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 74.88,
          "end": 77.13,
          "en": "because it will hold my server component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 77.13,
          "end": 78.57,
          "en": "And this is a good practice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 78.57,
          "end": 82.14,
          "en": "having the folder name equal your component name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 82.14,
          "end": 84.99,
          "en": "And each component typically should have its own folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 84.99,
          "end": 88.41,
          "en": "though it's not a hard rule, but generally it makes sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 88.41,
          "end": 90.36,
          "en": "So here in the server folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 90.36,
          "end": 92.55,
          "en": "I will add my server component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 92.55,
          "end": 97.11,
          "en": "Now a good naming convention is to have servers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 97.11,
          "end": 99.27000000000001,
          "en": "or the name of your component first,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 99.27000000000001,
          "end": 102.33,
          "en": "then a dot, and then component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 102.33,
          "end": 105.24000000000001,
          "en": "We will later learn that there are other building blocks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 105.24000000000001,
          "end": 107.19,
          "en": "in an Angular application too.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 107.19,
          "end": 109.08,
          "en": "So by using file names like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 109.08,
          "end": 112.14,
          "en": "it's very easy to see what's inside the file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 112.14,
          "end": 115.47,
          "en": "And very important, don't forget to add dot ts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 115.47,
          "end": 116.64,
          "en": "so for type script,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 116.64,
          "end": 120.06,
          "en": "because this is what we will write this component in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 120.06,
          "end": 123.06,
          "en": "So now we got an empty file for our new component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 123.06,
          "end": 124.923,
          "en": "How do we create a component now?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 126.06,
          "end": 129.45,
          "en": "First of all, a component simply is just a class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 129.45,
          "end": 130.65,
          "en": "a TypeScript class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 130.65,
          "end": 133.56,
          "en": "So that Angular is able to instantiate it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 133.56,
          "end": 136.71,
          "en": "to create objects based on the blueprint we set up here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 136.71,
          "end": 137.88,
          "en": "you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 137.88,
          "end": 139.47,
          "en": "So let's export this class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 139.47,
          "end": 141.96,
          "en": "so that we can use it outside of this file too,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 141.96,
          "end": 143.88,
          "en": "because as I mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 143.88,
          "end": 146.55,
          "en": "we're going to use our component in the app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 146.55,
          "end": 148.74,
          "en": "for example, to add it there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 148.74,
          "end": 151.2,
          "en": "So we will add a class here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 151.2,
          "end": 154.92000000000002,
          "en": "and this class should now be named server component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 154.92000000000002,
          "end": 156.72,
          "en": "Again, the naming convention here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 156.72,
          "end": 159.9,
          "en": "have the name of the component first, server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 159.9,
          "end": 161.82,
          "en": "and then also the description component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 161.82,
          "end": 164.31,
          "en": "because later we will also learn about other parts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 164.31,
          "end": 167.52,
          "en": "which might then be named differently in the Angular app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 167.52,
          "end": 169.11,
          "en": "This is our class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 169.11,
          "end": 171.27,
          "en": "and right now it's a normal TypeScript class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 171.27,
          "end": 173.43,
          "en": "Nothing special about it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 173.43,
          "end": 174.93,
          "en": "We can't use it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 174.93,
          "end": 178.23,
          "en": "Angular doesn't have all the information it requires.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 178.23,
          "end": 180.3,
          "en": "So we should add something to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 180.3,
          "end": 182.79,
          "en": "which tells Angular that this is not only",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 182.79,
          "end": 184.71,
          "en": "a normal TypeScript class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 184.71,
          "end": 187.95,
          "en": "but instead something special, a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 187.95,
          "end": 190.59,
          "en": "We do this by adding a special decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 190.59,
          "end": 193.05,
          "en": "Decorators are a TypeScript feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 193.05,
          "end": 196.74,
          "en": "which allow you to enhance your classes, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 196.74,
          "end": 199.47,
          "en": "Enhance elements you use in your code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 199.47,
          "end": 200.94,
          "en": "It's not restricted to classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 200.94,
          "end": 203.61,
          "en": "but here we will use a class decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 203.61,
          "end": 205.86,
          "en": "It's the component decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 205.86,
          "end": 207.93,
          "en": "And decorators are always attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 207.93,
          "end": 210.84,
          "en": "by adding an at sign in front of them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 210.84,
          "end": 213.36,
          "en": "Now, this component, decorator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 213.36,
          "end": 216.54,
          "en": "is not something TypeScript knows from the start,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 216.54,
          "end": 218.94,
          "en": "so we have to import it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 218.94,
          "end": 221.55,
          "en": "We have to add a import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 221.55,
          "end": 226.14,
          "en": "and this import now needs to give us access to components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 226.14,
          "end": 227.57999999999998,
          "en": "So we need to import component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 227.57999999999998,
          "end": 228.87,
          "en": "Between curly braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 228.87,
          "end": 231.45,
          "en": "because from the file where we're going to import this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 231.45,
          "end": 233.73,
          "en": "we could import other parts too.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 233.73,
          "end": 235.95,
          "en": "So we have to specifically pick the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 235.95,
          "end": 237.6,
          "en": "by using the syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 237.6,
          "end": 239.76,
          "en": "And then it's from.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 239.76,
          "end": 242.85,
          "en": "And now the package where we import component from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 242.85,
          "end": 246.6,
          "en": "is at Angular core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 246.6,
          "end": 248.94,
          "en": "Now Angular ships with a couple of packages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 248.94,
          "end": 251.37,
          "en": "where it basically groups its functionalities.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 251.37,
          "end": 253.2,
          "en": "And the core package, as the name implies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 253.2,
          "end": 255.84,
          "en": "gives us access to some of the core functionalities",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 255.84,
          "end": 257.25,
          "en": "of Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 257.25,
          "end": 259.5,
          "en": "So with that, we import that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 259.5,
          "end": 262.95,
          "en": "Nowadays, at component decorator is known to type script,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 262.95,
          "end": 266.46,
          "en": "so when it parses this file and compiles it to JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 266.46,
          "end": 268.68,
          "en": "that is able to understand it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 268.68,
          "end": 270.9,
          "en": "Now we need to pass a JavaScript object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 270.9,
          "end": 273.39,
          "en": "to this component decorator to configure it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 273.39,
          "end": 275.07,
          "en": "because without any configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 275.07,
          "end": 278.15999999999997,
          "en": "it's still not that valuable to Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 278.15999999999997,
          "end": 281.22,
          "en": "But here we can set up some important information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 281.22,
          "end": 284.1,
          "en": "which will be stored as metadata for this class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 284.1,
          "end": 285.45,
          "en": "in the background then,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 285.45,
          "end": 288.93,
          "en": "which will tell Angular what to do with this class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 288.93,
          "end": 293.34000000000003,
          "en": "And one important information piece is the selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 293.34000000000003,
          "end": 296.28,
          "en": "So basically, the HTML tag,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 296.28,
          "end": 299.04,
          "en": "by which you're able to use this component later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 299.04,
          "end": 301.26,
          "en": "in your other components templates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 301.26,
          "end": 303.6,
          "en": "We will see this in action soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 303.6,
          "end": 305.7,
          "en": "The selector should be a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 305.7,
          "end": 309.06,
          "en": "and here you may set up any name you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 309.06,
          "end": 312,
          "en": "but you should make sure that it is a unique selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 312,
          "end": 315.72,
          "en": "That you don't accidentally override a default HTML element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 315.72,
          "end": 317.25,
          "en": "or something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 317.25,
          "end": 320.79,
          "en": "So typically you prefix it with app, dash,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 320.79,
          "end": 322.74,
          "en": "and then a fitting name, like server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 322.74,
          "end": 325.2,
          "en": "because it's a server component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 325.2,
          "end": 327.87,
          "en": "This is my own selector by which I can now later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 327.87,
          "end": 332.7,
          "en": "use this component in my other components HTML files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 332.7,
          "end": 334.05,
          "en": "So with that's set up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 334.05,
          "end": 337.86,
          "en": "the other important piece we need to have is the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 337.86,
          "end": 341.82,
          "en": "And here, let's reference an other external file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 341.82,
          "end": 345.45,
          "en": "I'll come back to another alternative today, soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 345.45,
          "end": 349.08,
          "en": "And this external file, of course, needs to be created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 349.08,
          "end": 352.62,
          "en": "So in the same folder, I will create a server dot component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 352.62,
          "end": 355.11,
          "en": "and now, dot HTML file.",
          "zh": ""
